  m_text: 'An if runs the lines inside its braces only when its condition is true. other.CompareTag("Player") is true when the object that entered has the tag Player. Visitor 3 has that tag; Crate 3 is Untagged. Without the if, both objects would write the line.


    <b>Predict:</b> Crate 3 enters the zone. Does the line inside the if run?


    <b>Try:</b>

    1. Press Play, select Zone 3 and open Code Watch.

    2. Watch the if line and the line inside it as each object passes.

    3. Select Crate 3 and set its Tag to Player.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
